`Git author filter` is passed to `git log --author` (a regex). `Issue tracker` is one of `none`, `jira`, `github`, `linear`; when it is `none`, every tracker step in Neo's skills is skipped silently.

## Neo agent roster

Neo's scouts ship with the plugin: `neo:neo-git-scout` (git, PR and worktree recon), `neo:neo-repo-scout` (cross-project code exploration), `neo:neo-memory-curator` (notes and Engram hygiene). Optional scouts copied into `.claude/agents/` (issue tracker, infrastructure) are listed here when added. Each scout reads the playbooks it owns from `.claude/agents/agent-notes/playbooks/` at session start and appends distilled learnings at session end (see that directory's README.md for the scout-to-file map). Scouts never mutate projects, infrastructure, or trackers — real work is deployed via `/neo:neo-deploy`.

## Engram rules (apply in every session)

- Engram cannot auto-detect a project from this root (it holds many git repos). Neo always passes `project: "neo"` explicitly for its own orchestrator memory, and `all_projects: true` for cross-project recall.
- Save observations about a project under that project's canonical **Engram key** from the registry below. Never let a branch name, worktree folder, or product alias become an Engram project.
- Engram writes go through the MCP tools only (`mem_save`, `mem_session_summary`, ...) — never write to the Engram database file directly. Read-only SQL queries against it are allowed.

