Status values: `active` (touched in the last 30 days), `occasional` (last 180 days), `dormant` (older). Engram-only keys with no directory: `neo` (orchestrator). New repos: Engram key = directory name, lowercased. This registry is living documentation — update the row when a repo is added, renamed, or a tracker key is confirmed. Re-run `/neo:neo-init` to detect repos that appeared or disappeared.

## Worktree roots

Work in flight can live in three places — all must be swept for activity:

1. `{{WORKTREE_ROOT}}` — linked git worktrees, manual and Orca-managed (also visible via `git worktree list` in the parent repo).
2. `<repo>/.claude/worktrees/` — per-repo Claude Code worktrees.
3. The Orca live view: `orca worktree ps --json` reports per-worktree agent state, card status and linked PRs — state git cannot see. (Skip when Orca is `no`.)

## Deployment rule (Neo sessions only)

Neo never mutates a project from its own session. Real work is deployed with cwd inside the target project (see `/neo:neo-deploy`) so the project's own CLAUDE.md, agents, skills, `.mcp.json`, and review gates fully apply. Subagents launched from Neo are read-only and must read the target project's CLAUDE.md before drawing conclusions.

## Agent notes

Neo's durable work record lives in `.claude/agents/agent-notes/` — start at its `README.md` (the index). Dated notes go under `YYYY/MM/`, procedures under `runbooks/`, standing facts under `playbooks/`. An unindexed note does not exist.
